WEBVTT

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:16.410
Only three of you are running
under thirty minutes.

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:22.290
I'm impressed you're all 
able to run a 10K now, but...

00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:24.920
We still have three weeks until the qualifier.

00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:30.380
20km is the base distance for cross country,
but none of us will drop out.

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:36.700
On the track, I'm planning to push the build-up
runs we'd been holding back on this spring,

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:41.100
so we can finish the last
thousand meters in 2:50.

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:43.170
I'm impressed.

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:47.920
You got a bunch of total
amateurs to the qualifier.

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:52.970
That's more than good enough
to hold your own coaching lecture.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:55.890
Making it to the qualifier isn't our goal.

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:57.070
Well, yeah.

00:01:00.890 --> 00:01:05.570
My legs and hips are shot,
but I still have my experience.

00:01:05.570 --> 00:01:09.040
I'll tell you everything I can.

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:12.820
Anyway, qualifiers are...

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:22.380
Looks like your legs and hips still work.

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:37.950
<b><i>Run with the Wind</i></b>

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:56.940
<b>Kansei University</b>

00:02:55.520 --> 00:03:00.640
Kansei University honors 
the spirit of Matsudaira Sadanobu,

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:58.650
<b>Chairman's Office</b>

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:03.910
who promoted the Kansei Reforms.

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:08.070
We value both academics and athletics.

00:03:08.070 --> 00:03:10.290
Wow! That's us!

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:13.150
We're in the paper! Yay!

00:03:13.150 --> 00:03:16.980
I never thought I'd appear in a newspaper.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:20.470
<b>“Aiming For the Top”
10 men take on the Hakone Ekiden</b>

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:20.110
Okay, smile.

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:26.290
Since you haven't 
made it through the qualifier,

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:29.130
getting you into the sports
section might be difficult,

00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:31.520
but your attempt itself is captivating.

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:34.730
I'll have your story run 
in the local news section.

00:03:35.130 --> 00:03:37.190
Thank you!

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:40.610
<b>Yaokatsu</b>

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:43.780
<b>Chairman's Office</b>

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:47.410
We're all hoping you'll 
make it through the qualifier.

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:58.320
I wish I could run right now.

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:02.720
<b><i>Place of Destiny</i></b>

00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:05.680
My parents called.

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:07.540
They saw us in the paper.

00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:08.890
They were so excited.

00:04:08.890 --> 00:04:10.560
So did ours.

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:12.600
They yelled at us for throwing peace signs.

00:04:13.070 --> 00:04:17.060
My parents told me to smile more.

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:21.140
What are your parents like? I can't imagine it.

00:04:21.140 --> 00:04:24.690
They're normal. Normal,
with faces that look like mine.

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:29.910
What do you think my parents are?

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:33.970
Everyone's so devoted to their parents.

00:04:33.970 --> 00:04:34.840
Right?

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:36.750
I guess so.

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:42.690
Actually, we even received 
an interview request from Nippon TV.

00:04:42.690 --> 00:04:45.380
T-T-TV?!

00:04:46.030 --> 00:04:50.230
I didn't know, but the qualifier
is televised, too.

00:04:50.610 --> 00:04:57.920
They even broadcast interviews with
a handful of particularly notable schools.

00:04:57.920 --> 00:05:01.670
And we were chosen for that?

00:05:01.670 --> 00:05:04.240
That's great news.

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:06.100
I haven't responded yet, though.

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:07.360
Why not?!

00:05:07.890 --> 00:05:10.460
If the cameras prevented us
from focusing on the race,

00:05:10.460 --> 00:05:12.080
we'd be putting the cart before the horse.

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:13.400
Damn honor student!

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:15.000
We should accept their offer!

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:17.040
I want to be interviewed! 
I want to be on TV!

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:20.480
Well, it'll certainly be good
for promoting the team.

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:21.520
What do you think?

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:23.760
I don't care either way.

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:25.260
Me, neither.

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:28.600
I wonder if they'll send a lady reporter.

00:05:29.540 --> 00:05:31.840
We'll finally be popular with girls.

00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:34.010
This is insane, Jota.

00:05:34.010 --> 00:05:35.710
What should we do?

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:37.230
It's finally happening.

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:43.820
Are you okay with this?

00:05:44.260 --> 00:05:45.160
What?

00:05:45.160 --> 00:05:49.160
Won't appearing on TV cause trouble for you?

00:05:53.410 --> 00:05:55.510
Sorry. Shouldn't have asked.

00:05:57.020 --> 00:05:59.350
They're so young.

00:05:59.350 --> 00:06:00.140
Huh?

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:02.000
We're gonna be on TV.

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:03.340
What? That's amazing!

00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:04.690
I'll definitely be watching!

00:06:04.690 --> 00:06:07.420
Yuki, Shindo, Prince, get ready.

00:06:07.780 --> 00:06:08.870
Okay.

00:06:13.210 --> 00:06:16.880
My “maybe” became a “definitely” today.

00:06:17.700 --> 00:06:20.820
The twins and Hana?

00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:21.560
Yes.

00:06:21.890 --> 00:06:26.780
Didn't I tell you I made a discovery
when we were in the bath together?

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:28.740
That attitude.

00:06:29.600 --> 00:06:30.950
That atmosphere.

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:35.120
They're definitely those of a woman in love.

00:06:35.800 --> 00:06:38.850
There's no other reason she'd make that face.

00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:44.260
Hana definitely loves one of the twins.

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:47.740
Youth is beautiful, isn't it?

00:06:49.250 --> 00:06:52.100
Kakeru, Musa. Joji, Jota. Let's go.

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:53.510
Okay.

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:55.010
You got this!

00:06:56.470 --> 00:06:59.440
But which one?

00:07:00.950 --> 00:07:03.860
They're practically the same person.

00:07:04.460 --> 00:07:08.190
Yes, so it's one or the other.

00:07:21.570 --> 00:07:22.500
It's huge!

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:26.460
The Hakone qualifier starts
at the Self-Defense Force base,

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:29.120
adjacent to Showa Memorial Park.

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:33.610
We'll start by running two laps
around the airstrip and taxiway.

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:35.800
That's about five kilometers.

00:07:36.290 --> 00:07:39.770
Then we'll head out 
onto the road, pass the station,

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:42.260
and cross under the monorail bridge.

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:44.940
That's about ten kilometers.

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:48.400
The turnaround point is at 11.2 km.

00:07:48.760 --> 00:07:51.400
When we return to the park, 
we'll have run fifteen kilometers.

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:54.240
We'll run a lap through the hilly park.

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:56.530
The finish line is next to 
the Minna-no Harappa Field.

00:07:57.040 --> 00:07:58.290
How plain.

00:07:58.290 --> 00:08:00.950
I expected the finish line to be flashier.

00:08:00.950 --> 00:08:03.070
You'll see the day of the race.

00:08:03.070 --> 00:08:05.000
It won't matter if it's plain or flashy anymore.

00:08:10.180 --> 00:08:12.060
And they'll announce the results here?

00:08:12.060 --> 00:08:15.430
That's right. This is where
our destiny will be decided.

00:08:32.130 --> 00:08:34.200
Do you think I'm being soft?

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:35.030
Huh?

00:08:35.920 --> 00:08:38.500
Should I have made them run more?

00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:41.660
Before I sleep, while I'm eating,
when I'm in the bathroom.

00:08:43.390 --> 00:08:45.760
My doubts are constantly following me.

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:48.250
Should I have imposed 
more rules like a stronger school

00:08:48.250 --> 00:08:51.120
and forced them to run more?

00:08:54.230 --> 00:08:56.760
You can't force a person to run.

00:08:57.330 --> 00:09:01.070
The only thing that makes 
a person run is their own will. Right?

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:02.640
Yeah.

00:09:03.470 --> 00:09:07.550
I was constantly suffering
when I ran during high school.

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:10.360
I don't ever want to be
restricted like that again.

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:13.180
This time, I'll run of my own free will.

00:09:13.180 --> 00:09:16.940
Freely, far away, to the end of the world.

00:09:18.220 --> 00:09:20.270
We still have time.

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:23.540
Thanks.

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:26.690
People always want to be strong.

00:09:31.580 --> 00:09:33.670
We have two weeks until the qualifier.

00:09:33.990 --> 00:09:36.520
It's a battle of concentration now.

00:09:36.520 --> 00:09:40.800
We'll need to focus and exercise self-control,

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:43.770
so we can go into the qualifier
in top physical and mental shape.

00:09:44.370 --> 00:09:45.980
There's nothing to be afraid of.

00:09:46.660 --> 00:09:49.190
We've trained more than enough.

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:53.900
We just need to turn that pressure into
a rasp and polish our minds and bodies.

00:09:54.810 --> 00:09:59.630
Imagine yourself running as a beautiful
blade on the day of the qualifier

00:09:59.630 --> 00:10:03.410
and diligently polish
yourselves to a fine point.

00:10:05.380 --> 00:10:07.040
How poetic.

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:08.430
I understand, though.

00:10:08.430 --> 00:10:10.450
We should be like tempered katanas.

00:10:10.450 --> 00:10:13.620
We'll be screwed if we polish too much
and break before the race, though.

00:10:13.620 --> 00:10:15.030
That's right.

00:10:15.030 --> 00:10:18.590
Listen to your minds and bodies
and polish carefully.

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:23.560
Competitions are strange things,
and I don't just mean long-distance races.

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:32.020
<b>Incoming Call
Mom</b>

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:27.260
You've done the training.
All that's left is to run.

00:10:27.260 --> 00:10:30.770
Or so you'd think, but for some
reason, some runners self-destruct.

00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:37.840
Most things we call mistakes are the result
of pressure or weakness of the mind.

00:10:38.490 --> 00:10:40.130
No matter how much you practice,

00:10:40.130 --> 00:10:42.420
you can't stop the anxiety
from rising to the surface.

00:10:43.210 --> 00:10:47.060
No matter how certain you are,
you still can't erase your fear of failure.

00:10:47.550 --> 00:10:50.920
The more you polish something,
the more fragile it becomes,

00:10:51.440 --> 00:10:55.300
just as a little bit of dust
can ruin a delicate machine.

00:10:57.650 --> 00:11:02.660
So we must find strength. 
Unwavering strength.

00:11:03.460 --> 00:11:06.880
True strength, so we won't
be defeated by ourselves!

00:11:07.140 --> 00:11:08.220
Yeah!

00:11:14.270 --> 00:11:17.070
Should you be doing this
two days before the qualifier?

00:11:17.070 --> 00:11:18.920
This is how we do things.

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:21.250
Today is the last day!

00:11:21.250 --> 00:11:23.260
Tomorrow, we'll sit and wait for the next day!

00:11:23.260 --> 00:11:24.220
Yeah, yeah!

00:11:24.220 --> 00:11:27.010
It's time for a message from our coach.

00:11:27.010 --> 00:11:28.740
Who? Me?

00:11:28.740 --> 00:11:29.990
In that case...

00:11:30.660 --> 00:11:33.680
I'll share my secret to success.

00:11:35.280 --> 00:11:36.200
Finally!

00:11:36.200 --> 00:11:38.060
The coach removes the veil!

00:11:41.410 --> 00:11:44.510
Alternate using your left and right feet.

00:11:44.510 --> 00:11:48.390
Do that, and you'll eventually
arrive at the finish line.

00:11:48.390 --> 00:11:50.110
Thank you.

00:11:51.750 --> 00:11:52.980
That's all?!

00:11:53.950 --> 00:11:57.010
When are you going
to start acting like a coach?

00:11:57.010 --> 00:11:59.470
Wait! Please wait!

00:11:59.470 --> 00:12:00.830
Wait!

00:12:06.640 --> 00:12:07.760
He's asleep.

00:12:08.390 --> 00:12:09.750
What do you think, though?

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:13.810
You can't say it didn't feel like
it would be no exaggeration

00:12:13.810 --> 00:12:16.300
to say he spoke the truth.

00:12:16.300 --> 00:12:18.410
What the hell are you trying to say?

00:12:20.060 --> 00:12:21.540
What is it? A girl?

00:12:21.540 --> 00:12:23.020
Sorry.

00:12:23.620 --> 00:12:24.890
Just how carefree are you?

00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:33.810
Kakeru, could you bring up
some ice from downstairs?

00:12:34.720 --> 00:12:35.810
Okay.

00:12:37.080 --> 00:12:39.860
This has nothing to do with you.

00:12:39.860 --> 00:12:41.390
Why are you calling now?

00:12:42.790 --> 00:12:45.820
You're bothering me. I want to focus.

00:12:45.820 --> 00:12:46.860
Bye.

00:12:58.620 --> 00:13:00.660
My parents saw the paper.

00:13:00.660 --> 00:13:01.640
Oh.

00:13:02.190 --> 00:13:05.160
I haven't seen them in a while.

00:13:10.740 --> 00:13:12.040
Here.

00:13:13.410 --> 00:13:16.520
You can't have different track suits forever.

00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:20.190
Wow!

00:13:20.190 --> 00:13:24.240
They're a present from everyone
at the shopping center.

00:13:24.240 --> 00:13:26.980
Don't embarrass us.

00:13:26.980 --> 00:13:28.130
We won't!

00:13:50.260 --> 00:13:51.720
Hey!

00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:55.680
Today, we're taking our first step
towards winning the Hakone Ekiden!

00:13:56.210 --> 00:13:58.970
Win? Win?!

00:14:21.490 --> 00:14:24.390
Hey, is he a regular now?

00:14:24.390 --> 00:14:25.760
Isn't he a first-year?

00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:28.120
That doesn't matter today.

00:14:28.120 --> 00:14:31.080
I see. I guess not.

00:14:32.370 --> 00:14:35.110
You can't help but look
at the cheerleaders, huh?

00:14:40.330 --> 00:14:41.380
Yeah.

00:14:43.140 --> 00:14:48.720
Haiji said they'd make it if their
combined time was less than 10:12:00.

00:14:48.720 --> 00:14:52.370
That's just over an hour per person.

00:14:52.370 --> 00:14:54.640
Isn't it over 20 km?

00:14:54.640 --> 00:14:57.910
A full marathon takes over two hours.

00:14:57.910 --> 00:14:59.910
They'll have to run like professionals.

00:14:59.910 --> 00:15:02.850
That's just over three minutes per kilometer.

00:15:02.850 --> 00:15:04.090
There they are.

00:15:05.460 --> 00:15:09.280
As you can see, there are no landmarks.
It'll be tough to judge your distance.

00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:13.440
The weather's poor, and we
don't know how the race will go,

00:15:13.440 --> 00:15:16.260
but don't get dragged along by
runners recklessly charging ahead.

00:15:16.940 --> 00:15:18.740
Kakeru and I will run in front.

00:15:18.740 --> 00:15:21.610
Stay together and maintain
your own pace in the beginning.

00:15:22.560 --> 00:15:24.500
By the time we finish
one lap around the airstrip,

00:15:24.500 --> 00:15:26.940
a lot of guys should start to fall behind.

00:15:30.970 --> 00:15:32.840
I'll be sending signals during the race.

00:15:33.440 --> 00:15:34.870
Don't lose sight of each other.

00:15:37.790 --> 00:15:38.730
I'm glad.

00:15:39.840 --> 00:15:42.110
I'm glad it's the ten of us.

00:15:42.580 --> 00:15:44.620
We wouldn't be here 
if anyone had been missing.

00:15:44.620 --> 00:15:46.950
Don't make it sound like
the final episode of something.

00:15:46.950 --> 00:15:48.860
This is the starting line.

00:15:49.410 --> 00:15:50.130
You're right.

00:15:51.960 --> 00:15:54.880
There are different numbers
of guys wearing uniforms.

00:15:54.880 --> 00:15:56.410
I was wondering about that, too.

00:15:56.410 --> 00:15:58.260
They've got more than ten guys.

00:15:58.260 --> 00:16:03.230
A team can register up to 
fourteen runners for the qualifier.

00:16:03.230 --> 00:16:07.710
Then they'll reduce their numbers
to twelve based on their physical condition.

00:16:07.710 --> 00:16:13.530
What? So they calculate your total time
based on your ten fastest runners?

00:16:13.530 --> 00:16:18.140
Yeah. Teams with lots of runners
have two runners as insurance.

00:16:18.930 --> 00:16:21.930
So this is what they call a numbers game.

00:16:21.930 --> 00:16:25.360
It also means Kansei is finished
if a single one of their runners

00:16:25.360 --> 00:16:27.350
doesn't make it to the finish line.

00:16:30.530 --> 00:16:33.020
It's okay. They'll all come back.

00:16:33.610 --> 00:16:34.580
I know it.

00:16:44.460 --> 00:16:45.500
Prince.

00:16:46.580 --> 00:16:47.900
I'll do it.

00:16:49.020 --> 00:16:49.930
Okay.

00:16:54.980 --> 00:16:57.370
I'll do the best I can.

00:16:58.640 --> 00:16:59.440
Okay.

00:17:00.270 --> 00:17:04.080
<i>Runners, please gather at the starting line.</i>

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:08.020
<i>Runners, please gather 
at the starting line. Gather round.</i>

00:17:08.020 --> 00:17:08.880
Let's go.

00:17:15.450 --> 00:17:19.140
<i>Line up by school. By school.</i>

00:17:19.550 --> 00:17:23.190
<i>Teito Univesity. Saikyo University.</i>

00:17:23.190 --> 00:17:24.850
<i>Tokyo Sport University.</i>

00:17:27.280 --> 00:17:30.920
Isn't our starting position
kind of a big handicap?

00:17:30.920 --> 00:17:33.670
It's based on performance. We can't complain.

00:17:33.670 --> 00:17:35.280
They really are different.

00:17:35.600 --> 00:17:39.730
Even if they weren't seeded, the people
who ran at Hakone last year feel different.

00:17:39.730 --> 00:17:40.670
Yes.

00:17:41.240 --> 00:17:43.620
We're just as good.

00:17:54.970 --> 00:17:56.360
I forgot.

00:17:56.360 --> 00:17:57.430
Forgot what?

00:18:00.170 --> 00:18:01.900
The mountains of Hakone are?

00:18:05.510 --> 00:18:07.140
The steepest in the world.

00:18:08.740 --> 00:18:11.020
Starting in thirty seconds.

00:18:17.220 --> 00:18:18.360
Starting in ten,

00:18:18.360 --> 00:18:19.320
nine,

00:18:19.320 --> 00:18:20.280
eight,

00:18:20.280 --> 00:18:21.240
seven,

00:18:21.240 --> 00:18:22.200
six,

00:18:22.200 --> 00:18:23.160
five,

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:24.120
four,

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:25.080
three,

00:18:25.080 --> 00:18:26.040
two,

00:18:26.040 --> 00:18:27.000
one.

00:18:38.800 --> 00:18:41.660
Go, Kansei University!

00:18:41.660 --> 00:18:43.930
Go!

00:18:52.090 --> 00:18:54.270
Finish the first five kilometers in 3:10 each.

00:18:54.270 --> 00:18:57.140
After that, use your own judgment.

00:19:01.620 --> 00:19:04.870
Just two laps of this makes me feel faint.

00:19:06.370 --> 00:19:08.370
Huh? Where's Hanako?

00:19:09.490 --> 00:19:11.790
The runners are starting their second lap!

00:19:11.790 --> 00:19:13.330
Is everyone ready?

00:19:14.860 --> 00:19:17.710
Sorry. Excuse me. Sorry.

00:19:26.060 --> 00:19:28.520
The lead pack's pace is 2:49!

00:19:33.810 --> 00:19:36.440
The lead pack's pace is 2:49!

00:19:36.440 --> 00:19:38.340
Don't let them drag you ahead!

00:19:41.390 --> 00:19:42.540
Please don't lose...

00:19:59.580 --> 00:20:00.510
Go.

00:20:21.530 --> 00:20:23.240
They're coming!

